{:theorem
 {:id :theorem,
  :statement
  "Let $S \\subseteq [n]$ and let $X_S = \\bigotimes_{i \\in S} X_i \\otimes \\bigotimes_{i \\notin S} I_i$. Then: $T^{\\otimes n} X_S (T^{\\otimes n})^\\dagger = \\frac{1}{2^{|S|/2}} \\sum_{R \\subseteq S} \\omega_R \\cdot X_{S \\setminus R} Y_R I_{S^c}$ where all $2^{|S|}$ resulting Paulis have weight $|S|$.",
  :content-hash "78ff26e5cd7700f1"},
 :obligations [],
 :archived-nodes {},
 :external-refs {},
 :nodes
 {:1-l4a001
  {:statement
   "By Lemma 3 (T Gate Conjugation): $T X T^\\dagger = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(X + Y)$ and $T I T^\\dagger = I$.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "31072fe45c1f2d5a",
   :display-order 1,
   :type :assumption,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :assumption,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-l4a001,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{}},
  :1-l4a002
  {:statement
   "For $X_S = \\bigotimes_{i \\in S} X_i \\otimes \\bigotimes_{i \\notin S} I_i$, using tensor product properties: $T^{\\otimes n} X_S (T^{\\otimes n})^\\dagger = \\bigotimes_{i \\in S} (T X T^\\dagger) \\otimes \\bigotimes_{i \\notin S} (T I T^\\dagger) = \\bigotimes_{i \\in S} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(X + Y) \\otimes \\bigotimes_{i \\notin S} I$.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "7e602899de05888e",
   :display-order 2,
   :type :claim,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :substitution,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-l4a002,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{:1-l4a001}},
  :1-l4a003
  {:statement
   "Expanding the tensor product over $i \\in S$: $\\bigotimes_{i \\in S} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(X_i + Y_i) = \\frac{1}{2^{|S|/2}} \\bigotimes_{i \\in S}(X_i + Y_i) = \\frac{1}{2^{|S|/2}} \\sum_{R \\subseteq S} \\prod_{i \\in S \\setminus R} X_i \\prod_{j \\in R} Y_j$ where each term in the sum corresponds to a choice of subset $R \\subseteq S$ representing positions where $Y$ is chosen instead of $X$.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "8f2ed00c30892a73",
   :display-order 3,
   :type :claim,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :algebraic-rewrite,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-l4a003,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{:1-l4a002}},
  :1-l4a004
  {:statement
   "Each term $\\prod_{i \\in S \\setminus R} X_i \\prod_{j \\in R} Y_j$ is a Pauli operator with weight exactly $|S|$: there are $|S \\setminus R| + |R| = |S|$ non-identity factors, each being either $X$ or $Y$. The phases $\\omega_R$ arise from commutation relations $XY = iZ$ when reordering products, but do not affect the weight.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "0299ae4e84a28481",
   :display-order 4,
   :type :claim,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :algebraic-rewrite,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-l4a004,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{:1-l4a003}},
  :1-l4a005
  {:statement
   "The number of terms is $2^{|S|}$ (one for each subset $R \\subseteq S$), each with coefficient magnitude $\\frac{1}{2^{|S|/2}}$. The squared coefficient magnitudes are $\\frac{1}{2^{|S|}}$, summing to 1 over all $2^{|S|}$ terms.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "3ed6c094c5b2be6f",
   :display-order 5,
   :type :claim,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :algebraic-rewrite,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-l4a005,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{:1-l4a003}},
  :1-l4a006
  {:statement
   "Therefore $T^{\\otimes n} X_S (T^{\\otimes n})^\\dagger = \\frac{1}{2^{|S|/2}} \\sum_{R \\subseteq S} \\omega_R \\cdot X_{S \\setminus R} Y_R I_{S^c}$ where all $2^{|S|}$ resulting Paulis have weight $|S|$ and coefficients of equal magnitude $2^{-|S|/2}$. QED.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "3d020ca8b9d44961",
   :display-order 6,
